==English==

===Etymology===
{{label|en|onomatopoeia}}. Connected with {{m|en|splash}} and {{m|en|splish}} by vowel {{w|apophony}} (sound change); compare with {{w|Indo-European ablaut}} as in {{m|en|sing}}/{{m|en|sang}}/{{m|en|sung}}/{{m|en|song}}. Compare also {{m|en|slosh}}.

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|ɒʃ|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|es}}

# to make the sound of [[splash|splashing]]
# to [[traverse]] [[mushy]] or [[marshy]] wetlands
# to [[spill]] or [[spill over]]

